Upstream-Status: Pending
Exit: Drop when fdsdk resolves version detection for hatch-vcs-backed packages in the sandbox.
Subject: python3-urllib3: bypass setuptools-scm with PRETEND_VERSION

Build nksdr surfaced urllib3 as the next element hitting the chardet-
class failure. urllib3 uses hatchling with [tool.hatch.version]
source='vcs' which delegates to setuptools-scm -> vcs_versioning, same
as chardet (see 0011). urllib3 already carries fdsdk-local patches
(version.patch, setuptools_scm_version.patch) but they are insufficient
to avoid the git-describe timeout in the sandbox.

Setting both the UNQUALIFIED PRETEND_VERSION env vars (which 0011
proved work) and the dist-qualified variants. Version matches the
element's existing ref (2.7.0-0-g9a950b92...).

diff --git a/elements/components/python3-urllib3.bst b/elements/components/python3-urllib3.bst
--- a/elements/components/python3-urllib3.bst
+++ b/elements/components/python3-urllib3.bst
@@ -12,4 +12,11 @@ depends:
 variables:
   strip-binaries: ''

+environment:
+  # setuptools-scm#957 workaround: skip VCS version detection in sandbox.
+  SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION: "2.7.0"
+  VCS_VERSIONING_PRETEND_VERSION: "2.7.0"
+  SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_URLLIB3: "2.7.0"
+  VCS_VERSIONING_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_URLLIB3: "2.7.0"
+
